Subject: [PATCH] coff-rs6000: self-register standalone XMC_TC TOC entries

Some XCOFF producers, notably Go's linker, emit standalone XMC_TC csects
for TOC entries without using the classic assembler idiom where a hidden
TOC csect has a same-name R_POS relocation to the target symbol.  The
symbol-table scan in _bfd_xcoff_link_add_symbols only records toc_section
for that classic form, so these defined XMC_TC csects can reach
xcoff_reloc_type_toc with h->toc_section still unset and fail with
"TOC reloc ... with no TOC entry".

If the relocation target is itself a defined XMC_TC csect, use that csect's
own section as the TOC entry section.  Undefined/imported symbols and
compiler-created TOC entries keep the existing behavior.

--- a/bfd/coff-rs6000.c	2026-06-30 16:31:09.852071605 +0000
+++ b/bfd/coff-rs6000.c	2026-07-14 17:33:59.958031379 +0000
@@ -3120,6 +3120,19 @@
 
   if (h != NULL && h->smclas != XMC_TD)
     {
+      if (h->toc_section == NULL
+	  && h->smclas == XMC_TC
+	  && h->root.type == bfd_link_hash_defined)
+	{
+	  /* Some XCOFF producers, such as Go's linker, emit a standalone
+	     XMC_TC csect for a TOC entry without following the classic
+	     same-name R_POS idiom that the symbol-table scan in
+	     xcofflink.c uses to register h->toc_section.  If this symbol
+	     is itself a defined XMC_TC csect, its own section is the TOC
+	     entry section.  */
+	  h->toc_section = h->root.u.def.section;
+	}
+
       if (h->toc_section == NULL)
 	{
 	  _bfd_error_handler
